a closer look at the injuries wood  suffered in the crash and his chances  for recovery  we bring in cbs news medical contributor  dr david agus david good morning  tiger's doctors describe his injuries as  fractures affecting both the upper and  lower portions of the tibia and fibula  bones  they they say they inserted a rod into  the tibia  and his foot and ankles ankle were  stabilized with screws  and pins what exactly does that mean for  him  well you know obviously this was serious  trauma he got taken to a level one  trauma center ucla  uh harbor hospital which is an excellent  hospital  and we're very lucky and he's very lucky  over that you know i have this little  uh a man here and what you can see is  this front bone is the tibia  so tibia is the large bone you could  feel in front of your leg  and there are two fractures in it where  they had to put a rod in  with pins on either side to stabilize  this bone and then here in the ankle  we're also multiple bones fractured  where they put screws in  and they're able to keep it stabilized  for healing  the healing process here takes four to  six months but luckily  it's done the surgery now so so  you're talking about a four to six month  recovery for these injuries specifically  we don't know like he mentioned in in  carter's story  uh that he has problems with his back do  you think they'll likely be affected by  this as well  no no question i mean it's not just the  bones it's the muscles they mentioned in  the press  uh conference also that the muscles  around the legs  were traumatized and so that caused  swelling and they actually had to put a  slit in each of the muscles  to allow the pressure to be relieved so  it's going to take a while to retrain  these muscles to enable these bones to  heal  over the rod and to enable him to walk  again  so how long do you think that process  could take david  you know i mean it's only guessing i  mean obviously i don't know all of the  details but we're talking at least six  months of recovery here  um you know to be able to get to some  semblance of walking um  to playing a sport to playing golf i  just don't know enough  yeah all right dr david agus thank you  very much
 

